# Generated by Cargo
# will have compiled files and executables
debug
target

# These are backup files generated by rustfmt
**/*.rs.bk

# MSVC Windows builds of rustc generate these, which store debugging information
*.pdb

# Generated by cargo mutants
# Contains mutation testing data
**/mutants.out*/

# rustc will dump stack traces when hitting an internal compiler error to PWD
rustc-ice-*.txt

# RustRover
#  JetBrains specific template is maintained in a separate JetBrains.gitignore that can
#  be found at https://github.com/github/gitignore/blob/main/Global/JetBrains.gitignore
#  and can be added to the global gitignore or merged into this file.  For a more nuclear
#  option (not recommended) you can uncomment the following to ignore the entire idea folder.
#.idea/

# Internal architecture notes (see concepts/README.md), anchored to the repository root.
# ROADMAP.md is the spec of specs: every open item names its feature specification.
# `tests/concepts.rs` guards them and skips when the directory is absent, which is what CI sees.
#
# The third-party corpus — BNetzA Festlegungen, statutes, BSI technical guidelines, VDE FNN
# documents, BDEW formats, open-source reference implementations — lives at
# `concepts/reference/` and is covered by this line: fetched by scripts/fetch-references.sh,
# indexed in `concepts/REFERENCES.md`, and never redistributed from here.
/concepts/

# This project's own feature specifications, and the Spec Kit machinery that produces them:
# one `specs/NNN-slug/` per ROADMAP item, `.specify/memory/constitution.md`, the threatspec
# extension, and the `/speckit-*` skills. Same rule as `concepts/` — internal, and the
# published tree may not cite a path its reader does not have; `cargo test --test concepts`
# fails on one that does. Matching iec61850-kit, iec60870, hems and eebus.
/specs/
/.specify/
/.claude/
.DS_Store

# The local Python environment with pandapower for the oracle test (tests/pandapower_oracle.rs).
/.venv/
/site/public/
